texture_cache: the decoder and its uploads survive a refusal

An allocation refused on the TextureDecoder thread had nobody to catch it, and one piece of up to
214 MiB is what decoded_data asks for. A bad_alloc there now sets a failed flag before complete.
TickAsyncDecode then clears IsDecoding and drops the entry before any upload, so the collector can
free the image and the context does not leak. The same goes for the input vector on the GPU
thread (54 MiB for Ocarina's arrays), caught around QueueAsyncDecode.

The staging of a decoded image no longer throws either. A refused slice stays where it is and goes
next frame with the image still marked as decoding, so a slice that finds the stream ring busy and
the pool empty only waits. A refused zero fill leaves the image without its clear until the decode
lands.

A dropped decode leaves a texture black until the guest writes it again.

